Stop a storage install from borrowing the host's split APKs.

SYMPTOM
    A cloned Firebase app could reach its login screen but never obtained an FCM
    token on the OnePlus CPH2605 (Android 15). The container's microG -- installed
    by MicroGProvider through the storage path -- was recorded with *Google Play
    services'* split APKs: the 37 MB microG base.apk sat next to
    split_AdsDynamite_installtime.apk, split_MapsDynamite_installtime.apk,
    split_config.xxhdpi.apk and the rest of the host GMS split set. Both spots
    below fell back to the host's splitSourceDirs whenever a package brought no
    splitCodePaths of its own, which for a storage install is exactly the case
    that means "this APK has no splits".

    With that mixed package the guest bind failed. Logcat showed:

        W BActivityThread: makeApplication returned null, attempting fallback creation
        E BActivityThread: Error creating application: null
        E BActivityThread: Fallback application creation failed: null
        D BActivityThread: Creating minimal application wrapper
        E BActivityThread: Unable to instantiate service
            org.microg.gms.gcm.PushRegisterService: java.lang.NullPointerException:
            Attempt to invoke virtual method 'java.lang.Class
            java.lang.ClassLoader.loadClass(java.lang.String)' on a null object reference

    after which no microG service could start, so checkin never completed and no
    FCM token was issued. Deleting the stray split files instead made
    createPackageContext return null and the bind abort on
    "assert packageContext != null".

FIX
    CopyExecutor: only a FLAG_SYSTEM install (by name, from the host) borrows the
    host's split set. A storage install owns its splits; when it brought none, it
    has none.

    PackageManagerCompat.generateApplicationInfo: same rule for what the guest is
    told. A storage install also drops recorded split paths whose files are gone
    (the polluted containers repair themselves on the next scan), and with no
    usable splits the splitDir fields are explicitly cleared -- they are part of
    the persisted ApplicationInfo, so leaving them would keep feeding the guest a
    split path that no longer exists.

MEASURED
    Physical device, OnePlus CPH2605 / Android 15, minified app + this AAR:
    a fresh Cabex FX clone completed microG checkin (checkin.xml written) and
    stored a real FCM token in the guest app's preferences
    (flutter.current_fcm_token, f...:APA91b...). Evidence:
    evidence/physical-android15/fcm-cabexfx-fixed/.
